hing else  entirely  that's cool I mean this video is called  why I love Dragon Ball super so if you  want to disagree be sure to leave me a  comment down below Dragon Ball super is  not going to be perfect that's what I  told myself right before watching the  very first episode back on July 5th 2015  on March 25th 2018 I watched the very  last episode of Dragon Ball super that  felt incredibly strange to say just now  I mean super has sort of become an  enormous part of my life over the last  three years having watched it a week to  week writing about it and researching it  it's been no secret to me that the show  has had huge struggles during this time  on the air be it on the production side  or elsewhere the show hasn't been  perfect not by a longshot but for some  reason that doesn't matter to me  sitting beside my brother while watching  the last episode unfold before my eyes I  couldn't help but remember that during  this show has brought me on throughout  the years whether it be the ball of  anxiety and excitement I was moments  before the first episodes airing the  shock episode 5 brought to everyone  which ultimately led me to this online  animation community I'm part of today  the feeling of lying in bed is go who  screamed Kaioken trying to temper my  excitement lest I wake those sleeping  around me the countless theories  surrounding the identity of Goku black  the more crazy the better my  introduction to the Spanish side of  Dragon Balls community god bless you  ultra instinct shaggy completo and  countless other wonderful engaging  experiences that I got to share with you  all thanks to this show you  despite not being perfect while watching  the last episode I had a big dumb smile  plastered right across my face as Goku  and Frieza my two favorite characters  fought alongside one another to bring  universe 7 to victory and thanks to  things like the Internet this all felt  like a worldwide shared experience in  various countries across the world there  were giant screens set up in public  squares  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  now don't get me wrong I can point to  numerous instances where the show  falters melts and flat out makes no  sense quite easily but I can't help but  love it all the same three years ago I  found myself working a job I hated that  ruined my health my sleeping pattern and  afforded me a little time to see anyone  in my life I was miserable  shortly after dragonball returned and  inspired me to try something new a  youtube channel I named it totally not  marked because at the time I wanted to  be anyone other than me I can confirm  with absolute certainty that's no longer  the case and I am incredibly proud of  this little corner of the internet I've  built from nothing with you guys  Dragon Ball super isn't perfect but it  has afforded me just some random guy the  ability to talk showcase and discuss  what I love with almost 100,000 people  every week through Dragon Ball I've had  the honour of making wonderful new  friendships with the likes of anime Ajay  geek Tim 101 Masako axe and countless  others so while watching that last  episode as the chaos of the tournament  had concluded and the tone began to  shift I felt a feeling similar to what  Dragon Ball Z left me with as a child  similar not identical when I first saw  Dragon Ball Z I was 10 years old  it helped me an awkward shy kid to  socialize with other people my age and  find my footing in my formative years  when Dragon Ball Z ended it genuinely  felt as though a friend had left for  good if that makes any sense  when Dragon Ball super began I was 23 it  helped me find my way out of a dark  place through hard work perseverance and  determination it made me laugh it made  me leave for my seat with excitement and  it inspired me to follow my dreams be it  cruel struggled to keep up with Goku  Vegeta is trying to catch up some boxes  saying ningún or the countless wonderful  experiences I've shared with all of you  over these last few months and years  it's been one of the most eye-opening  magical experiences of my entire life  Dragon Ball just has something that sets  itself apart from every other form of  entertainment out there for me it  without fail turn me into a kid again  and any element of cynicism or nitpick  immediately took a backseat as I was  launched into this wondrous  impact thrill ride it's not perfect but  I couldn't help it I got caught up in  the gut punching earth shattering  screaming ducing supernova that was  Dragon Ball super  you  ie without reservation loved Dragon Ball  super and no matter what way I look at  it it just fills me with happiness  I love Dragon Ball super not because I  can't see anything wrong with it but I  love too much about it to care about the  bad as the episode began to wind down  and we were greeted for the last time  with the two characters many of us have  grown up with you might have felt  emotional had been filled with nostalgia  or indifference but I couldn't help but  look on with that same wide-eyed smile I  had when I was a kid  Dragon Ball super wasn't perfect but it  was more than good enough for me  [Music]  you  I want to take this opportunity to thank  all those who helped produce Dragon Ball  super behind the scenes through all of  its hardships you are the real heroes of  this series through all of the trials  and tribulations plaguing this animated  production they managed to deliver not  only the best ending this series has  seen in my opinion but also one of the  strongest if not these strongest  standalone episodes I have ever seen I  want to thank each and every one of you  for listening to me ramble on about this  I'm not gonna say goodbye to Dragon Ball  but until we meet again Goku matinee  [Music]  you  [Music]  you  you  [Music]  you  [Music]

